Fail-closed trigger

Two retryable S8 runtime cycles reported:

- 2026-08-30T18:38:52.016527Z
- 2026-08-30T19:30:26.713684Z

Safe classification:

- safe_exception_type: TelegramApiError
- safe_reason: S8_TELEGRAM_API_UNAVAILABLE
- sqlstate: null

Although later health probes were GREEN, the strict two-hour gate permits no runtime
error. The observation therefore cannot pass and no automatic retry is authorized.

Rollback execution

The first rollback attempt stopped before mutation because the Control Git index mode
was 0644. Ownership and both repositories were otherwise correct and clean. The mode
had been recreated by a Git status refresh that did not set GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0.

The already versioned normalize-index-modes action restored the narrow approved mode
0660. The versioned rollback then completed successfully and reported:

- S8_PUBLIC_TELEGRAM_ROLLBACK_GREEN
- waitlist_data_preserved=true

The observer subsequently stopped fail-closed with REPOSITORY_SHA_DRIFT because the
rollback intentionally returned the application repository to the S7 release.

